@startuml
title CycleFar — Upload, replace or remove a ride file

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Rider
boundary "RideFilesController" as Controller
control "RideFileAttacher" as Attacher
control "Fit::Reader" as Reader
control "RideCalculator +\nNormalizedPower" as Calculator
control "RideFileRemover" as Remover
entity "WorkoutActivity" as Activity
database "PostgreSQL" as Database
collections "Active Storage\nlocal disk volume" as Storage

== Upload or replace (FBK-004) ==
Rider -> Controller: POST ride_file (multipart FIT file)
Controller -> Database: load workout through the rider's active plan
alt workout outside the active plan or owned by another rider
  Controller --> Rider: 404
end
Controller -> Attacher: call(workout, file)
Attacher -> Attacher: reject missing file or > 10 MB before reading
Attacher -> Reader: samples(bytes)
note right of Reader
  Parsed outside the plan lock.
  Checks header, .FIT signature, CRC and
  activity file type; decodes record samples
  (time, power, heart rate, speed).
end note
alt invalid, truncated, corrupt or non-activity file
  Reader --> Attacher: InvalidFile
  Attacher --> Controller: Rejected with readable message
  Controller --> Rider: redirect to workout detail with alert; nothing stored
end
Reader --> Attacher: samples
group transaction under plan lock
  Attacher -> Database: lock plan; reload workout
  alt workout not completed
    Attacher --> Controller: Rejected
    Controller --> Rider: redirect with alert
  end
  Attacher -> Calculator: call(samples, completed_ftp_watts)
  Calculator --> Attacher: moving/elapsed time, power, NP, IF, TSS, work, heart rate
  Attacher -> Activity: create, or replace metrics on existing record
  Activity -> Database: save row; trigger requires completed parent, no reparenting
  Activity -> Storage: store FIT file (blob + attachment)
end
opt replacing an earlier file
  Activity -> Storage: purge previous blob through Solid Queue
end
Controller --> Rider: redirect to workout detail; note a date mismatch if any

== View ==
Rider -> Controller: GET workout detail or calendar
note over Controller
  Detail shows planned against ridden metrics.
  Calendar cards show ridden TSS when power exists.
end note

== Remove ==
Rider -> Controller: DELETE ride_file (confirmed)
Controller -> Database: load workout through the rider's active plan
Controller -> Remover: call(workout)
group transaction under plan lock
  Remover -> Database: lock plan; reload workout
  Remover -> Activity: destroy (if present)
  Activity -> Database: delete row and attachment
end
Activity -> Storage: purge blob through Solid Queue
Controller --> Rider: redirect to workout detail

note over Calculator, Storage
  The completed workout's structure, snapshot, metrics and feedback
  are never written; ridden metrics use its frozen completion FTP.
  Ridden metrics are display only: no weekly totals, load limits,
  feedback evaluation, adaptation or Intervals.icu sync reads them.
end note
@enduml
